by-the-informational-relationships-amo--52a77799b51d\",\"claim-each-particular-conscious-experience-is-specified-by-the-current-activity-values--ef679659733b\"],\"source_ids\":[\"source-05-self-awareness-self-regulation-and-self-transcendence-s-art-a-framework-for-unde-w2005022581--615ee4e1923f\",\"source-01-an-information-integration-theory-of-consciousness-w2114900706--09db8f102f39\"]},{\"topic_id\":\"topic-benefits-safety-and-evidence-limits\",\"title\":\"Mindfulness Benefits, Safety, and Evidence Limits\",\"structure_type\":\"wiki\",\"sections\":[\"S-ART-related claims describe reported benefits of mindfulness or compassion practices for clinical symptoms, executive function, physiological relaxed alertness, immune markers, and stress reactivity, but the broader research critique warns against treating these findings as uniformly strong clinical evidence.\",\"The critical mindfulness source emphasizes immature clinical evidence, heterogeneous interventions, mixed condition-dependent efficacy, weak controls, and under-assessed adverse effects. These constraints qualify how reported benefits should be interpreted.\",\"A synthesis page should present potential benefits and potential harms together: adverse effects, contraindications, opportunity costs, dosage, practice quality, participant history, and clinical monitoring are part of the same evidence-assessment problem.\"],\"claim_ids\":[\"claim-short-mindfulness-interventions-have-been-reported-to-improve-clinical-symptoms--38a77abb1074\",\"claim-meditation-practice-is-associated-with-physiological-profiles-of-relaxed-alertne--a46fa752f290\",\"claim-mindfulness-based-stress-reduction-and-compassion-meditation-have-been-reported--d470d02dbd8f\",\"claim-future-mindfulness-research-needs-longitudinal-measurement-of-s-art-subcomponent--a2496826340c\",\"claim-clinical-evidence-remains-preliminary--117717456958\",\"claim-mindfulness-based-interventions-show-mixed-and-condition-dependent-clinical-effi--ada76b44a400\",\"